2 cups of flour are needed to make 12 cookies, so the amount of flour needed per cookie is: flour/cookie = 2 cups / 12 cookies = 1/6 cup/cookie Carla is making 36 cookies today and 30 cookies tomorrow. Thus, the total number of cookies is 36 + 30 = 66 cookies.  Since each cookie needs 1/6 cup of flour, the total amount of flour needed is: flour = 66 cookies * (1/6 cup/cookie) = 66/6 cups = 11 cups.
Therefore, Carla will need 11 cups of flour to bake all the cookies.

\boxed{11}

